[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\draw[thick] (0,0) rectangle (4,4);
\node[below] at (2,-0.1) {$1\text{ km} = 1000\text{ m}$};
\node[rotate=90] at (-0.5,2) {$1\text{ km} = 1000\text{ m}$};
\node at (2,2) {$1\text{ km}^2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Each side of this square is $1000$ m long.
How many $\text{m}^2$ are there in $1\text{ km}^2$?
